## Slide 2 — Our Solution

### LunarSight: A Visual Tool for Exploring Candidate Sites

LunarSight is a research prototype designed to make the lunar South Pole easier to explore and analyze.

Its intended capabilities include:

- Displaying a 3D Moon with selected south-polar research points.
- Showing candidate coordinates and their scientific sources.
- Visualizing the apparent positions of the Sun and Earth.
- Supporting future terrain-aware visibility analysis.
- Showing assumptions and model limitations alongside results.

